      "math_academy_id": "e-12359",
      "problem": "Find a fraction that's equivalent to $1 \\div (-7).$",
      "worked_solution": "We have to divide a positive number $({\\color{blue}{1}})$ by a negative one $({\\color{red}{-7}}).$ So the result will be negative:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14152110/assets/dbbab0c71c897276bea288ef526943a59162d43255dd81c5ed2b81f63a8aac3a.svg)\n\nTo write down the number that goes in the box, recall that \n\n$$\n1 \\div 7 = \\dfrac{1}{7}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}{1}} \\div {\\color{red}{(-7)}} = {\\color{red}-\\dfrac{1}{7}}.\n$$",
